---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PageHero, Prose, Section } from '../components/ds';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Provisa"
  description="What Provisa collects, why, and how to control it: sign-in via Google, GitHub, or Microsoft; the product-update mailing list; nothing else."
  contact={false}
>
  <PageHero
    crumbs={[{ label: 'Provisa', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
    eyebrow="Last updated August 31, 2026"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lede="Provisa is a single product, operated by Kenneth Stott. This page covers the provisa.dev website and the sign-in used by the Provisa application. It does not cover data you load into your own Provisa deployment — that data is yours, stays in your infrastructure, and is never seen by us."
  />

  <Section tone="surface" label="Privacy policy">
    <Prose>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>Two things, and nothing beyond them:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Sign-in to the Provisa application.</strong> When you sign in with Google, GitHub, or Microsoft, we request only your
          <strong>name, email address, and profile picture</strong> (scopes: <code>profile</code>, <code>email</code>). We use this solely to
          create and authenticate your account and to know who is asking when a query runs. We never request access to your files, contacts,
          calendar, or any other data those providers hold.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Product-update mailing list.</strong> If you submit the “Keep me posted” form on this site, we store the
          <strong>name and email address</strong> you enter, for the sole purpose of emailing you product updates.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we don’t collect</h2>
      <p>
        No advertising trackers, no third-party analytics pixels, no cross-site tracking. We don’t sell, rent, or share your data with any
        third party for their own marketing purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it’s stored</h2>
      <p>
        Sign-in identities are managed by Firebase Authentication (Google Cloud). Mailing-list entries are stored in a private Cloudflare D1
        database that only the Provisa operator can access. Both providers process data under their own security and compliance commitments as
        our data sub-processors; neither is authorized to use it for their own purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Sign-in data persists for as long as your account exists; delete your account and it is removed. Mailing-list entries persist until you
        unsubscribe or ask us to remove them — every email includes an unsubscribe link, and the address is de-duplicated so you’re only ever
        stored once.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Sign in with any of the three supported providers, or self-host with your own auth if you’re running Provisa on your own infrastructure.</li>
        <li>Unsubscribe from the mailing list at any time via the link in any email.</li>
        <li>Ask us to access, correct, export, or delete your data — email us and we’ll handle it directly, no ticket queue.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy, or a request to access, correct, or delete your data:
        <a href="mailto:privacy@provisa.dev">privacy@provisa.dev</a>. General support: <a href="mailto:support@provisa.dev">support@provisa.dev</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
